    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190-a2">

                <pb facs="0337" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg225"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Consul at Hankau to Consul-General
                        Martin</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June 17,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir and Dear Colleague</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inform you that the area which extends from the end of the original Japanese
                    concession at this port 150 chang northward along the river and 120 chang to the
                    west from the bank of the river, having been leased in perpetuity to His
                    Imperial Majesty’s Government in virtue of an agreement signed on the 9th
                    February last by the Taot’ai and myself and subsequently sanctioned by the
                    respective superiors, this consulate is under instructions to start registry of
                    ownership of the land situated within the above limits.</p>
                <p>I therefore have the honor to request that you will notify such of your nationals
                    or protégés as may possess land on the said concession extension to produce
                    their title deeds at this consulate for examination and registration before or
                    on the 16th of August, 1907, and thereby to agree to their property being
                    included in the Japanese concession extension.</p>
                <p>Thanking you in anticipation,</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">K. Midzuno.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
